WEBVTT

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:03.640
My passionate idol activities,

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:07.220
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:10.550
So far on Aikatsu:

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:14.700
A new idol school called Dream Academy, or DreAca for short, has sprung up.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.740
A face-off concert between them and us at Starlight Academy was held,

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:22.000
where Otoshiro Seira-chan made her debut.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:26.580
With Saegusa Kii handling her production, she performed a Constellation Appeal.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:31.130
Then, Ichigo returned from America.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.930
Unbelievably, Ichigo was also able to perform a Constellation Appeal.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:49.540
No matter how you look at it, 
she's really something special.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:51.360
Seira-chan's a really cool girl, isn't she?

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.990
Oh, but she's kinda cute too...

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:55.570
She's like coolly cute.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.950
She just made her debut, but she's already super popular.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:01.950
There's just this air about her.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:03.390
I know!

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:04.800
She was brilliant!

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.120
Her Constellation Appeal, too.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:09.710
Yeah. And it felt like one of those "it just happened" things that you always do, Ichigo.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.300
"It just happened" things?

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.930
Yeah, like it was really effortless. {fuck this}{adl;ihg}

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:16.460
"It just happened", as in "somehow the Constellation Appeal just happened".

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:20.310
She's a tough one, that Otoshiro Seira.

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:21.180
Yeah.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.340
This is gonna be great!

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:25.510
We'll get to do Aikatsu together!

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.570
I'm sure she's thinking the same thing.

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:31.890
Thinking that Hoshimiya Ichigo will be tough to beat, I mean.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:34.090
Yeah, definitely.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.740
She's a tough one, that Hoshimiya Ichigo-chan.

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:16.130
Research, research!

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:19.820
Go, go, go for it! Fight, fight, fight!

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:21.380
Let's, let's, go, go!

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:23.470
Oh, oh, oh!

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:26.950
I'll do anything for Seira!

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:28.490
You're sure into it today.

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:30.440
We can't afford to lose to her.

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:32.740
You know it. {said it}

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:37.690
Ah!

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:39.530
I can't believe it!

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:41.320
What can't you believe?

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:47.620
You know how Ichigo-chan lost to Kanzaki Mizuki in last year's Starlight Queen Cup?

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:51.830
Apparently the margin of victory was extremely small.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:52.970
I can believe that.

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:55.460
She managed to perform that Constellation Appeal the other day, after all.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.100
And I heard that she performed a Special Appeal during her entrance audition.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:03:59.990
Really?

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:01.470
So you did some research of your own.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.600
I knew you'd be curious about Ichigo-chan.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.850
I guess you could say that.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:11.610
What I'm most curious about is her mysterious year in America.

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:14.100
I'm going to try to find out what she did over there.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:18.630
She must've had a really important reason to leave for America

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:20.610
despite being at the peak of her popularity.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.190
That's probably true.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:23.370
Wow, wow, wow!

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:24.160
What is it?

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.730
He saying he's giving up. {or she}

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:32.160
He says that even though he found a lot of articles, it's too difficult to pick out the truth. {what doesn't make sense is your line}

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.630
You talk like the computer is one of your friends.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:37.110
He is!

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.000
They're all my friends!

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.510
So what do the articles say?

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:43.760
Hmm, let's see here...

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.560
"Ichigo jumped through flaming hoops at a circus."

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:47.180
Excuse me?

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:50.890
Hot, hot, hot!

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.870
"Ichigo became a star on Christmas."

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:54.520
What?

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.520
Merry Christmas!

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:02.440
"Ichigo rode on an orca's back in the middle of the ocean."

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:02.900
Pardon?

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:07.200
Orca!

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:09.300
What an interesting girl.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.410
That information is all useless, though.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.450
I know, I know, I know!

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:16.230
From the data he gave us, we can get the general picture,

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:17.420
but something's still off.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:20.800
Did Hoshimiya Ichigo just spend the whole year goofing off?

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:23.070
I wonder about that.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:26.600
We shouldn't jump to conclusions without investigating further.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:27.570
You're right.

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:28.800
Which means...

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:31.030
...we have to go ask her in person!

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:36.050
Hey, I'm fine with going to Hoshimiya Ichigo's house,

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:37.560
but why aren't you coming with me?

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:39.110
If you were here, we—

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:40.570
I can't, I can't, I can't!

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:43.670
I'm too busy collecting more data.

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:45.320
At least give me directions, then.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:47.110
Ok-ok-okay!

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.330
Another helping, please!

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:56.010
Onee-chan, that's your third bowl, you know!

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:58.330
It's been so long since I've had Mama's kinpira veggies, after all.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:01.460
Ichigo, you seem a lot more like an older sister than before.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:02.400
Really?

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:03.840
How so?

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:06.590
Maybe because you had to cook for yourself over there,

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:09.090
the way you carry yourself has changed.

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:12.970
You've gotten more older sister-like as an idol, too.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:15.600
Have there really been that many idol debuts lately?

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:16.870
A ton!

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:19.480
Especially from Dream Academy!

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.670
I know about them. DreAca, right?

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:23.980
And speaking of idols,

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:27.090
a new cafe just opened right by our house.

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:29.000
It really piqued my interest.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.290
Why?

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:32.090
It gave off the scent of an idol!

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:34.290
Then let's go check!

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:35.750
I want a parfait for dessert, anyway.

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:38.000
You're going to eat more?

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:45.940
There's no doubt about it.

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:48.780
There's an idol hiding in here somewhere!

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:51.510
Raichi, you're a lot more like Aoi now.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:52.770
Here.

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:54.510
A strawberry parfait and a lychee parfait.

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:56.530
Sorry for the wait.

00:06:56.530 --> 00:06:57.660
Wow.

00:06:57.660 --> 00:06:59.020
Your voice is beautiful.

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:02.520
Thank you, Hoshimiya Ichigo-chan.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.110
I'm flattered you know me.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:09.530
You see, my daughter is a huge fan of yours.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:12.320
{Wow!}

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:14.990
Come on, Noelle.

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:17.330
This is a rare chance. Say hi to her.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:22.440
H-Hello.

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:23.580
Hello.

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:26.430
Raichi, you too.

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:27.170
Huh.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:29.170
Oh?

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:36.220
So the rumor about you being 
Ichigo-chan's brother was true!

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:37.260
Yeah.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:40.060
She just transferred into the class next to mine.

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:42.850
Nice to meet you. I'm Otoshiro Noelle.

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:47.820
Wait, don't tell me you're related to the Otoshiro Seira-chan who just debuted!

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:49.170
I'm her little sister.

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:50.030
I'm her father.

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:50.860
I'm her mother.

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:55.400
Super coincidence!

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:58.200
I never would've guessed Seira-chan's family would live so close by!

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:01.880
Hey, Noelle-chan! Tell us about your sister!

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:04.850
I want to know more about Seira-chan too!

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:07.840
Onee-chan...

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:12.080
She's really good at the piano, guitar, and violin.

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:14.090
She also has absolute pitch.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:16.240
Absolute pitch?

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:20.820
It means she can determine what note any sound is just by hearing it once.

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:21.480
Right?

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:22.400
Yeah.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:23.890
What else?

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:28.580
When Onee-chan sings, the music seems to shine and sparkle.

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:29.480
She's that kind of person.

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:30.900
Noelle-chan.

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:33.240
You must love your sister a lot.

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:34.340
I do!

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:40.550
Kii, I'm there.

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:44.000
Wait, this place is really close to my house.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.600
I guess it is.

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:48.750
Alright! Mission start!

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:50.120
Roger.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:55.540
I'll buy a bento, and then nonchalantly ask about Hoshimiya Ichigo while I wait.

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:57.670
And remember, the "nonchalantly" part is super important!

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:58.630
Got it.

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:03.810
Ah, welcome!

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:05.520
Two seaweed bentos, please.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:07.750
Sure.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:09.510
Just a moment.

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:11.530
Then, while I'm waiting...

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:14.400
Could you tell me about Hoshimiya Ichigo? {would}

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:17.950
That was like the complete opposite of nonchalant.

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:30.810
Otoshiro Seira-chan, right?

00:09:30.810 --> 00:09:32.390
Please have a seat.

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:33.800
How do you know who I am?

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:35.800
I saw your concert.

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:40.470
Both your voice and your appeals were brilliant.

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:42.350
Thank you very much.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:45.140
I'm so happy I could break out in song.

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:47.850
Thanks for waiting. Here's your seaweed bento.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:50.010
Thank you.

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:51.660
I'm so sorry.

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:54.630
Too bad you had to come when Ichigo was out of the house.

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:55.790
Oh, don't mind it.

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:57.310
Want some miso soup?

00:09:58.530 --> 00:09:59.670
Please!

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:05.340
It's delicious!

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:08.550
I've never had a seaweed bento this good!

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:10.110
Thank you.

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:10.790
I wonder what it is.

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:15.010
The seaweed is good, but there's something about the rice that makes it spectacular!

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:17.170
It tastes completely different from normal rice!

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:20.030
There are lots of different kinds of rice.

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:22.610
Different strains have different tastes. {breeds? cultivars? brands?}{I think strain is fine}

00:10:22.610 --> 00:10:24.180
There are different ways to cook it, too.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.320
I see.

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:29.440
I didn't know there was so much to rice.

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:32.580
The difference between types is like the difference between <i>do</i> and <i>re</i>.

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:36.440
Ichigo can tell exactly what kind of rice she's eating with a single bite.

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:39.200
That's just like absolute pitch.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:40.220
Huh?

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:42.610
You're good, Hoshimiya Ichigo.

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:43.740
You're so interesting.

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:46.460
I'm going to have that ability too!

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:47.800
Absolute taste!

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:51.590
Seira-chan, you're such a funny girl.

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:53.960
Good afternoon.

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:57.030
I heard Ichigo-chan's come back from America.

00:10:57.030 --> 00:10:59.450
Yes, she has.

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:01.170
She just got back.

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:01.970
Is she in?

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:04.470
She stepped out for a bit.

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:05.890
That's unfortunate.

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:08.690
I really wanted her autograph too.

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:09.620
Me too.

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:11.720
Oh my.

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:14.980
I'm so happy!

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:17.740
I can't believe I'm getting Ichigo-chan's autograph!

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:20.060
I want Seira-chan's autograph.

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:22.320
Autographs from when an idol debuts are super rare!

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:24.840
I don't know if she even has one.

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.950
She just made her debut, and she's a really shy person.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:33.960
I'm sure Seira-chan would give every fan an autograph with all her feelings in it.

00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:35.040
Yeah.

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:37.630
I'm so happy.

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:39.470
Could you sign one more for me?

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:41.220
Gladly.

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:46.100
Here, I'm done.

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:48.150
Thank you, Ichigo-chan!

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:49.390
I'll treasure this forever!

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:51.510
Thank you, too.

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:54.120
Thank you, Seira-chan.

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:55.790
I'll be cheering for you.

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:57.150
Thank you.

00:11:57.520 --> 00:12:00.430
I'll ask Ichigo to contact you when she gets back.

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:02.780
Sorry we kept you so long.

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:06.030
I don't mind. I enjoyed it.

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:13.850
Ichigo-chan's mom was pretty cute.

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:14.290
Yeah.

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:16.310
So how did it go?

00:12:16.310 --> 00:12:17.930
How was Ichigo-chan's house?

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:19.800
My stomach's really full.

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:24.600
Meaning, I got to know so much about Hoshimiya Ichigo that my stomach is full.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:26.070
She's really someone to be reckoned with.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:27.810
Right, right, right?!

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:31.310
I'm looking forward to it, though.

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:33.810
I can't wait to sing with her on stage!

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:39.860
What? Seira-chan was here?!

00:12:40.270 --> 00:12:42.210
Too bad we missed her.

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:43.570
It's tragic, really.

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:48.970
Seira-chan said that she wanted to be able to distinguish between types of rice like you can, Ichigo.

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:50.080
Really?

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:53.540
Then I'll have to try to get absolute pitch!

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:55.740
That sounds really hard.

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:59.090
Aren't you happy you have a new friend now?

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:00.590
Yeah!

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:08.300
Oh yeah, and Seira-chan ate an entire large seaweed bento and even asked for extra miso soup!

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:09.930
Apparently she really likes pickled vegetables! {It would ring better if we just used "shibazuke" though}

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:10.470
Really?!

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:13.430
Seira-chan likes pickled vegetables?

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:15.160
You get excited at the strangest things...

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:16.230
Ah...

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:19.720
I want to sing with Seira-chan already.

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:23.290
That's one thing about Ichigo that never changes.

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:26.990
The idol world will be shaken, now that Ichigo's back!

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:29.410
Let's do our best! {arighom}

00:13:40.390 --> 00:13:41.340
You called?

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:43.880
You're sure pumped up today.

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:44.340
Good!

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:47.280
I know it's sudden, but there's a new concert happening.

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:48.090
Concert?

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:55.100
The Swing Rock brand's Swing Idol Live is going to be held at Dream Academy.

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:57.730
They've asked you to participate.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:01.500
Swing Rock's the brand that Seira-chan wears, right?

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:02.110
Yes!

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:05.240
Naturally, Otoshiro Seira will be participating, too.

00:14:06.230 --> 00:14:07.610
I'll do it, I'll do it!

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:08.900
Please let me do it!

00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:10.490
Naturally. No problem.

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:14.750
You'll have to wear Swing Rock clothes, though. Is that okay with you?

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:15.870
Of course!

00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:18.250
I'm relieved to hear that.

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:21.660
We don't have much time before the concert,

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:24.000
but let's rock the Aikatsu world!

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:25.060
Let's!

00:14:31.820 --> 00:14:33.490
I wonder where Seira-chan is.

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:34.680
You made it.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:36.820
Welcome to the Swing Idol Live.

00:14:36.820 --> 00:14:38.690
Welcome to Dream Academy.

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:41.390
I was here just a few days ago, actually.

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:44.190
I'm happy to see you again.

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:45.570
Same here.

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:46.490
Me too.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:48.450
Oh, there you are!

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:51.010
Ichigo-chan and Seira-chan.

00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:53.870
What kind of performance are you planning to give today?

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:57.480
A performance that'll bring the brightest smiles to everyone's faces.

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:59.870
That's my goal as an idol.

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:01.480
And you, Ichigo-chan?

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:05.390
I want to bring smiles to everyone's faces too.

00:15:05.390 --> 00:15:08.230
Oh, and I want to fill up their stomachs too.

00:15:08.230 --> 00:15:09.380
Their stomachs?

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:12.830
When your stomach is full, 
you're full of happiness too! {or "your heart is full"}

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:14.010
I see!

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:22.170
Ichigo-chan.

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:23.740
I came to cheer you on.

00:15:23.740 --> 00:15:24.570
Noelle-chan!

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:26.690
Thanks for coming.

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:29.020
Where's your sister? Did you see her already?

00:15:29.020 --> 00:15:29.960
Nope.

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:33.370
She's probably meditating or something right now.

00:15:35.190 --> 00:15:36.200
I see.

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.580
Ichigo-chan, do you mind me being here?

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:40.600
Udon and seaweed!

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:44.650
"Udon to nori."

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:45.880
"Don't worry."

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:48.410
It means "don't worry about it". {ertoguntrg}{"It means "I don't mind.""}

00:15:54.730 --> 00:15:57.020
Being with you makes me smile.

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:59.020
It's like when I listen to my sister sing.

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:00.150
Really?

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:05.020
When I was younger, I was frail and sick all the time.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:08.400
But whenever I felt down, Onee-chan's singing cheered me up.

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.900
She's a great sister, isn't she?

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:12.970
Yeah!

00:16:14.420 --> 00:16:16.260
Bite down and gyoza!

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:17.930
Whoa, shumai?

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:22.460
Alright!

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:24.200
Seira-chan!

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:29.510
Thanks.

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:31.170
You put a smile on my sister's face.

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:32.410
Huh?

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:36.930
Noelle-chan said her sister's singing always cheered her up.

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:41.000
But the only thing that's ever made her smile from her heart

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.940
was seeing you sing on TV.

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:48.350
She loved how you'd fall down and get right back up, singing with all your heart.

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:51.190
That's why I'm thanking you.

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:55.370
But...

00:16:55.890 --> 00:16:56.840
I won't lose.

00:16:57.690 --> 00:17:00.740
As an idol, I want to be better than you!

00:17:04.470 --> 00:17:05.960
Seira-chan!

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:08.130
Let's give it all we've got.

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:09.210
Yeah!

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:32.000
Wow!

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:33.800
They both did Constellation Appeals!

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:34.290
They did.

00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:38.560
In the end, who fired up the audience the most?

00:20:38.560 --> 00:20:42.420
The winner of the Swing Idol Live is...

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:52.140
Otoshiro Seira!

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:56.920
Otoshiro Seira has won against Hoshimiya Ichigo!

00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:05.070
Looks like I lost!

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:07.820
But that felt great!

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:10.620
Wasn't it fun, Seira-chan?

00:21:16.190 --> 00:21:17.580
Good job, good job!

00:21:18.070 --> 00:21:19.750
Good for you, Seira!

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:21.380
You beat Ichigo-chan!

00:21:21.740 --> 00:21:23.380
Did I really win?

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:27.840
For some reason, I don't feel like I won.

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:33.690
I feel like Hoshimiya Ichigo's voice resonated more than mine did.

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:35.350
Hers shone brilliantly.

00:21:36.070 --> 00:21:38.710
That's why I didn't actually win.

00:21:38.710 --> 00:21:39.780
Seira...

00:21:44.340 --> 00:21:45.150
Kii?

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:47.360
I'm going to try even harder!

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:49.820
And just you watch, Seira!

00:21:50.900 --> 00:21:53.290
I'll pro-pro-produce you to the top!

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:58.710
I'm counting on you, producer. {capital?}

00:21:58.710 --> 00:21:59.750
Yeah!

00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:07.760
You did great, Ichigo.

00:22:08.310 --> 00:22:12.260
It's really hard to beat Otoshiro Seira at anything rock-related,

00:22:12.650 --> 00:22:15.520
but you looked like you really had fun out there.

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:17.760
Yeah, it was tons of fun!

00:22:17.760 --> 00:22:19.220
That's what's most important.

00:22:19.220 --> 00:22:19.770
Right!

00:23:55.880 --> 00:23:57.660
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:23:58.980 --> 00:24:01.590
Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do is actually Italian.

00:24:01.590 --> 00:24:03.270
What is it in Japanese?

00:24:03.270 --> 00:24:04.690
Ha-ni-ho-he-to-i-ro-ha. {what I'm guessing is that they started at G for some reason...}

00:24:04.690 --> 00:24:05.630
I see!

00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:07.310
It's different, isn't it?

00:24:08.050 --> 00:24:09.800
Music scales up!

00:24:10.670 --> 00:24:12.490
It's important for an idol to have a good smile.

00:24:12.490 --> 00:24:15.300
I'll teach you how to look cute in pictures.

00:24:15.300 --> 00:24:16.600
Yay!

00:24:16.600 --> 00:24:18.770
I'll practice it right away!

00:24:18.770 --> 00:24:19.990
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:19.990 --> 00:24:21.310
The secret to smiling.

00:24:21.310 --> 00:24:25.310
Always passionate, idol activities!
